<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <!--
        PHASE 2 - MANUFACTURING categories.

            Raw Materials  ->  [Production]  ->  Finished Goods
                                                      |
                                                    Waste

        These sit ALONGSIDE the trading categories from somgreen_config, not
        instead of them. That separation is the whole point: bought-in goods
        point at Sales/COGS - Merchandise, manufactured cartons point at
        Sales/COGS - Manufactured Goods, and the P&L shows trading margin and
        manufacturing margin as two readable lines rather than one blended
        number that flatters whichever side is weaker.

        AVCO for the same reasons as the trading categories - see
        somgreen_config/data/product_category.xml. AVCO is not a preference
        here: mrp_account/models/mrp_production.py:_cal_price sets the finished
        move's cost from actual order cost only `if cost_method in ('fifo',
        'average')`. Under standard costing the carton is valued at its standard,
        the real packing cost never lands, and the conversion-cost mechanism
        below goes dead.

        VALUATION IS LEFT ON 'manual_periodic' HERE AND FLIPPED TO AUTOMATED IN
        THE UI, exactly as in somgreen_config. The reason is the same but the
        failure mode is worse.

        somgreen_config cannot write 'real_time' because its accounts do not
        exist yet and _check_valuation_accounts raises. Here they do exist, so
        writing 'real_time' does NOT raise - and that is the problem. The
        constraint (stock_account/models/product.py:977) checks only the three
        MANDATORY fields, and each is company_dependent: with no value on the
        category they resolve through the company ir.default fallbacks, which
        Phase 1 pointed at the TRADING accounts. So the module would install
        clean, the categories would look configured, and every manufacturing
        stock move would post to 105100 Merchandise Inventory until someone
        noticed. Silent, not loud - which is why the Phase 1 safeguard is kept.

        Note the Production Account is NOT covered by that constraint at all.
        mrp_account adds property_stock_account_production_cost_id to the
        category's account list but not to the mandatory list, so leaving it
        blank blocks nothing - it silently falls back to the stock input
        account. Set it explicitly on all three categories.

        ACCOUNTS DO NOT INHERIT FROM A PARENT CATEGORY, and these three are
        flat, so wire each one directly. Per category, in ONE save:

            Stock Valuation    105200 / 105300 / 105400
            Stock Input        106100 Stock Interim - Received
            Stock Output       106200 Stock Interim - Delivered
            Production Account 105600 Cost of Production
            Stock Journal      Inventory Valuation
            Income             401200 Sales - Manufactured Goods
            Expense            501200 COGS - Manufactured Goods
            Costing Method     Average Cost (AVCO)
            Inventory Valuation  Automated

        noupdate="1": the accountant wires those accounts and flips valuation by
        hand, and `-u somgreen_mrp` must not reset the fields back to the blank
        values below. Same reasoning as somgreen_config.
    -->

    <!-- Everything consumed in packing: tissue packs, boxes, tape, labels,
         stretch wrap. One bucket, no sub-categories - they are all consumed the
         same way and valued the same way, and splitting them would only add
         categories to keep wired. -->
    <record id="categ_raw" model="product.category">
        <field name="name">Raw Materials</field>
        <field name="parent_id" ref="product.product_category_all"/>
        <field name="property_cost_method">average</field>
        <field name="property_valuation">manual_periodic</field>
    </record>

    <!-- Finished cartons, produced not bought. Automated valuation is mandatory
         on THIS one in particular: mrp_account's _post_labour short-circuits on
         `if mo.product_id.valuation != 'real_time': continue`, so under manual
         valuation the work-center cost is never posted to the GL at all. -->
    <record id="categ_finished" model="product.category">
        <field name="name">Finished Goods</field>
        <field name="parent_id" ref="product.product_category_all"/>
        <field name="property_cost_method">average</field>
        <field name="property_valuation">manual_periodic</field>
    </record>

    <!-- Damaged packs and rejects: scrapped, not a routine by-product. Packing
         has no by-product, so By-Products can stay switched off. -->
    <record id="categ_byproduct_waste" model="product.category">
        <field name="name">Waste</field>
        <field name="parent_id" ref="product.product_category_all"/>
        <field name="property_cost_method">average</field>
        <field name="property_valuation">manual_periodic</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
